Prefer monochrome symbol fonts over color emoji for text-presentation glyphs.

cosmic-text's font fallback lists place the color emoji font ahead of (macOS) or
mismatch the family name of (unix) the monochrome symbol fonts. Codepoints that
default to *text* presentation but also exist in the color emoji font -- notably
U+23FA (BLACK CIRCLE FOR RECORD), which Claude Code prints as its message/tool
bullet -- therefore resolve to the color emoji font and render as a filled color
block with a solid background.

The glyph lives in Noto Sans Symbols 2, whose real family name contains a space
("Noto Sans Symbols 2"). fontdb matches family names exactly:

  * macos.rs lists no symbol font at all before "Apple Color Emoji" -- add the
    Noto symbol fonts (both spellings of the "2" variant) ahead of it.
  * unix.rs already lists symbol fonts before "Noto Color Emoji" but only the
    unspaced "Noto Sans Symbols2", which never matches -- add the spaced name.

These symbol fonts cover technical/text symbols but not pictographic emoji, so
real emoji (e.g. U+1F534) still resolve to the color emoji font.

--- a/src/font/fallback/macos.rs
+++ b/src/font/fallback/macos.rs
@@ -31,6 +31,17 @@
     &[
         ".SF NS",
         "Menlo",
+        // Prefer monochrome symbol fonts for text-presentation glyphs (notably
+        // U+23FA, the bullet Claude Code prints) so they don't fall through to
+        // Apple Color Emoji and render as a filled color block. Mirrors the
+        // symbol fallbacks unix.rs lists ahead of "Noto Color Emoji". Note the
+        // glyph lives in "Noto Sans Symbols 2" (the family name has a space;
+        // the unspaced spelling is kept too in case fontdb reports it). These
+        // cover technical/text symbols but not pictographic emoji, so real
+        // emoji (e.g. U+1F534) still resolve to Apple Color Emoji just below.
+        "Noto Sans Symbols",
+        "Noto Sans Symbols 2",
+        "Noto Sans Symbols2",
         "Apple Color Emoji",
         "Geneva",
         "Arial Unicode MS",
--- a/src/font/fallback/unix.rs
+++ b/src/font/fallback/unix.rs
@@ -42,6 +42,11 @@
         /* Symbols fallbacks */
         "Noto Sans Symbols",
         "Noto Sans Symbols2",
+        // The Noto Sans Symbols 2 family name actually contains a space; the
+        // unspaced spelling above doesn't match it in fontdb. U+23FA (Claude
+        // Code's bullet) lives here, so without this it falls through to the
+        // color emoji font and renders as a filled block.
+        "Noto Sans Symbols 2",
         /* Emoji fallbacks*/
         "Noto Color Emoji",
         //TODO: Add CJK script here for doublewides?
